WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.820
Movie the age of alchemy. In the hushed whispers of the ancient world a craft was born one steeped in mystique and intrigue

00:08.440 --> 00:12.680
Alchemy its cradle was the sun-drenched sands of Hellenistic Egypt

00:13.320 --> 00:17.080
around the fourth century BC a time when the wisdom of the Greeks

00:17.680 --> 00:23.560
Egyptians and later Islamic philosophers entwined to form a tapestry of thought ripe with potential

00:23.760 --> 00:28.480
This was not merely a craft but a philosophy a quest for the essence of existence itself

00:29.040 --> 00:32.320
Alchemy sought transformation not just of matter but of the soul

00:32.840 --> 00:40.040
It was a dance with the elements a flirtation with the boundaries of the known its practitioners the alchemists

00:40.360 --> 00:42.920
whispered of turning lead into gold of

00:43.520 --> 00:49.240
discovering the elixir of life and of unlocking the mysteries of the cosmos a craft a

00:49.640 --> 00:56.480
philosophy a quest and so in the crucible of ancient thought alchemy began its transformative journey as

00:57.240 --> 01:04.120
Centuries rolled on alchemy entered its golden age its influence spreading from Alexandria to the Islamic world and beyond

01:04.520 --> 01:12.920
this period of cultural intellectual and scientific growth saw alchemy transform from a mystical endeavor to a more systematic discipline a

01:13.400 --> 01:17.560
driving force in this transformation was Jabir Ibn Hayyan a

01:18.000 --> 01:22.120
Polymath hailing from the heart of the Islamic world known as the father of chemistry

01:22.760 --> 01:26.340
Jabir developed many of the basic processes still in use today

01:27.220 --> 01:30.600
distillation crystallization calcination sublimation and

01:31.000 --> 01:39.060
Evaporation are all attributed to his pioneering work his innovative apparatus like the Alembic are still recognizable in modern

01:39.200 --> 01:43.360
Laboratories, but alchemy's golden age wasn't confined to the Islamic world

01:43.600 --> 01:49.560
It spread its gilded wings to reach the courtyards of Europe during the Middle Ages and Renaissance here

01:49.600 --> 01:53.160
It would be further refined and developed by figures like Paracelsus

01:53.640 --> 02:00.800
The Swiss physician and alchemist who challenged traditional medical practices with a chemical approach to diagnosis and treatment

02:01.520 --> 02:05.800
Even Isaac Newton renowned for his contributions to physics and mathematics

02:06.480 --> 02:08.400
Dabbled in the art of alchemy

02:08.400 --> 02:16.520
His secretive work in this field much of it discovered posthumously only serves to underscore alchemy's far-reaching influence during its golden age

02:17.000 --> 02:19.400
From the sands of the Middle East to the courts of Europe

02:20.040 --> 02:27.680
Alchemy was leaving an indelible mark on the world as the whispers of alchemy echoed through the ages a new voice began to rise

02:28.120 --> 02:31.160
the voice of reason the voice of science as

02:31.880 --> 02:38.320
The sands of time slipped away the age of alchemy began to fade making way for a new era an

02:38.600 --> 02:45.760
Era where the mystical and spiritual pursuits of alchemy were slowly replaced by empirical and systematic approaches

02:46.040 --> 02:51.920
This was the dawn of the Scientific Revolution a period that marked the birth of modern chemistry

02:52.720 --> 02:59.600
Enter Robert Boyle an Irish natural philosopher who is often regarded as the first modern chemist

02:59.740 --> 03:05.840
He was the one who bid goodbye to the arcane practices of alchemy and welcomed the experimental method

03:06.240 --> 03:13.640
Boyle's law which describes the inversely proportional relationship between the absolute pressure and volume of a gas

03:14.080 --> 03:17.600
Still holds a prominent place in the realm of modern chemistry

03:17.960 --> 03:24.200
Then came Antoine Lavoisier the French chemist who is celebrated as the father of modern chemistry

03:24.320 --> 03:26.320
He was the one who introduced a new

03:26.960 --> 03:28.960
nomenclature system for chemical substances

03:29.840 --> 03:32.720
Moving away from the allegorical language of alchemy

03:33.160 --> 03:40.000
His work on combustion and the conservation of mass set the foundation for the chemical equations we use today

03:41.000 --> 03:46.000
Despite the transition the legacy of alchemy persists in modern chemistry

03:46.480 --> 03:53.880
the symbols the pursuit of purification and the transformation of substances all bear the fingerprints of alchemy and

03:54.760 --> 04:01.120
So from the mystical depths of alchemy emerged the clear empirical voice of modern chemistry

04:01.480 --> 04:07.080
Although the whispers of alchemy have faded its echoes can still be heard in the halls of science today

04:07.360 --> 04:14.160
This ancient practice steeped in mystery and intrigue was the foundation upon which modern chemistry was built

04:14.360 --> 04:20.200
It was alchemists who first began to ponder the nature of matter to question to experiment

04:20.640 --> 04:24.760
This insatiable curiosity has been passed down from generation to generation

04:25.840 --> 04:28.680
fueling the scientific exploration we witnessed today

04:29.520 --> 04:34.200
alchemy's pursuit of transformation both literal and metaphorical continues to inspire

04:34.560 --> 04:36.560
Its essence lies in the belief of

04:37.280 --> 04:41.360
Potentiality the idea that one thing can become another that change is possible

04:42.000 --> 04:47.600
This philosophy is not just confined to laboratories. It extends to every facet of our lives

04:48.360 --> 04:52.720
Encouraging us to constantly strive for improvement for growth in the end

04:53.400 --> 04:59.040
alchemy's greatest transformation was not of lead into gold but of mysticism into science a

04:59.840 --> 05:02.080
Transformation that continues to shape our world today

